predef: "l2src/lmx.h.lm1"
predef: "l2src/lmx_arena.h.lm1"
predef: "l2src/lmx_scratch.h.lm1"

# One activation over the selected complete callable Structure. Its declared
# fields and executable role nodes remain in the graph; activation working values,
# argument places and temporaries live only in the C frame/scratch lifetime.
# The native word and source graph are not rewritten by interpretation.
#
# Frame nodes are ordinary Structures whose child0 is a shared physical role
# record. Remaining children are operands; no runtime source names are resolved.
# Entry accepts an existing Structure, including an empty executable body. Reached
# roles execute in body order; unknown reached roles report UNSUPPORTED.
# Explicit CALL/EXEC selects an occurrence and dispatches its native word or walks
# that occurrence. Merely returning or passing a descriptor never executes it.
#
# Declared own cells are loaded into per-activation working rows. Bare assignment
# changes the working value and dirty bit; ordinary call/exit checkpoints publish
# only dirty rows. Explicit physical place operations do not reload or dirty them.
#
# VALUES. Each recursive evaluation produces one LmxWalkValue: presence, closed
# source type, and either an exact-width numeric member or an opaque held reference.
# A null reference is present; void/absent has present=0. Physical pointer cells
# are loaded once at producers. A reference that happens to point to another pointer
# cell is not implicitly followed. Descriptor values retain their actual identity.
# ADDRESS resolves a physical LmxWalkPlace without a value load, publication or dirty
# change; ELEM places select backing storage before char/pointer value projection.
# CALL/PRIM transport uses addresses of declared-width value storage. Zero storage
# denotes absence, while nonzero pointer storage can hold null. ARG's type witness
# loads into stable callee-owned storage, independent of caller/scratch transport.
# Numeric results are copied by their declared width before scratch is rewound;
# references retain their payload and source category without allocating a graph.
# THE WORKING STATE (§7b, steps/working-state-7b.md; book §12 `#dynamic`, §14; Lingvamyxa spec 21.5,
# 21.6 -- the model above, restored by the author's decision, docs/new_parts/dirty.md; the k.2 reading
# "cells ARE the graph, no working copies" is withdrawn).  At entry the activation loads the own fields its
# body uses by a bare name into the frame's working table (LmxWalkFrame.work: rows taken from the scratch
# store after the activation's mark, linked in the order they were made): one row per field -- where its
# slot is, what it holds.  The set is not stored anywhere (the author, 2026-09-28: no auxiliary structures
# in the graph beside the graph itself and what the source makes): it is the code's own -- every OWN,
# OWN_OF and SET_OF node the body holds, found by walking down from its steps through the Structures each
# node owns (lmx_walk_load_code).  OWN and OWN_OF read the row, SET and SET_OF write it and mark it dirty;
# a slot with no row is the translator's broken promise, said as "lmx: invariant: an own field used but
# not loaded" (X1).
# The publication (lmx_walk_publish) writes the dirty rows into their slots in row order and unmarks
# them: at CALL after its arguments, at PRIM_PUB after its operands, and when the activation ends --
# RET after its value, a fall-off, a throw that leaves.  AT, PUT, PUT_REF, OF and PUT_OF are explicit
# graph operations and never see the table: a write through them leaves the working value as it is.
# Nothing is reloaded after a call, and a clean row is never written back.  Activation state lives
# only on LmxWalkFrame and in its scratch slice; nothing precomputes or caches a field set (k.4).
# MUL/DIV/MOD: [mul|div|mod, a, b]; typed numeric result; div/mod 0 -> INVALID.
# PUT_OF (-177 c4 / D-54): [put_of, struct-expr, slot, value]; holder evaluated.
# D-105 (Q39): OF [of, struct-expr, slot, req] and PUT_OF [put_of, struct-expr, slot, value, req] --
# a non-null req is the named Structure the place is typed with: the slot is an EDGE into the
# `implements` table's correspondence (K01): below req's width it is req's own field (an explicit
# `[N]name` use), from width to 2*width-1 the LAST half of field slot - width (a bare `name` use,
# the value's last occurrence of it).  lmx_implements_slot resolves the edge to the value's own
# slot; no record = INVALID.
# lmx_walk_slot refuses an OP-node holder (X1). receiveMessage take (-177 c1): PRIM record whose fn is lmx_walk_mail_take (nargs 0);
# Empty inbox yields a present null reference under its declared result contract.
# lmx_walk_admit / lmx_walk_admit_letter consume two reference-value storage inputs;
# letter admits its payload. YES preserves the reference; NO throws IMPLEMENTS.
# lmx_walk_merge_model is the existing explicit runtime merge callback; this
# carrier description does not define source declaration/call classification.
# CALL/EXEC child3 and PRIM.signature share the ordinary two-part contract:
# child0 is the ordered input-witness Structure; child1 is an empty return part
# for void, or contains one result witness. The contract is declared metadata,
# never inferred from supplied operands, used ARG nodes or a callable's data child0.
#
#   ret     [ret, value?]                 return an optional typed value
#   call    [call, code, data, contract, catch, actuals...]
#             code/data identify the selected complete callable occurrence;
#             its native word selects native adapter or ordinary walk.
#   exec    [exec, 0, target-expression, contract, catch, actuals...]
#             evaluate the actual target once, then use the same dispatch.
#   lit     [lit, typed-cell]             snapshot a literal's typed value
#   own     [own, holder, slot]           read the activation's working value
#   own_of  [own_of, holder-expression, slot]  read a hosted working value
#   arg     [arg, ordinal, fallback?, type-witness]  present input or lexical fallback
#   set_arg [set_arg, ordinal, value, type-witness]  write callee-owned input storage
#   at      [at, holder, slot]            read physical declared storage
#   of      [of, descriptor-expression, slot, model?]  physical path read
#   deref   [deref, held-reference, referent-witness]  select the referent's place
#   address [address, place-expression, pointer-witness]  address of real storage
#   put     [put, place-expression, value]  select place, receive value, physical store
#   put_ref [put_ref, holder, slot, descriptor]  replace a direct descriptor child
#   set     [set, own-node, value]        working assignment, mark dirty after reception
#   set_of  [set_of, holder-expression, slot, value]  hosted working assignment
#   prim_pub [prim_pub, record, catch, operands...]  publish after operands, then callback
#   add sub mul div mod lt eq [op, a, b]
#   if      [if, cond, then, else?]       then/else are bodies
#   while   [while, cond, body]
#
# The set of roles beyond RETURN and CALL and the operands of each are a carrier draft
# for probing the mechanism, not an L3 ISA (dev/graph_interp/BODY_NODES.md).
#
# QUALIFIED IMMUTABILITY.  The full `independent: const: immutable` receiver profile is
# itself an ordinary graph value.  LmxWalkContext carries its physical reference.  A
# candidate is immutable exactly when its address range's array carries that same profile
# reference; owner-local objects are protected and foreign ownership/sealing alone grant
# nothing.  The way OUT is closed while a body is prepared: `put`, `set`, or a primitive
# owner targeting that exact profile makes preparation INVALID.  Reading remains valid.
#
# This header describes the implemented carrier, not a second language grammar.
# Source eligibility/type resolution belongs to the translator. Reached malformed
# operands report INVALID; unknown roles report UNSUPPORTED. Empty bodies finish
# normally. Runtime callbacks retain their distinct status/throw propagation.
#

define: LMX_WALK_OK 0
# Malformed body tree, not a callable, a field reference that selects nothing, an own
# field that is not lexically inside M, a missing input.
define: LMX_WALK_INVALID 1
# A callable with no body node: nothing to walk.
define: LMX_WALK_NO_GRAPH 2
define: LMX_WALK_NOMEM 3
# An unknown reached executable role or an unsupported reached operation.
define: LMX_WALK_UNSUPPORTED 5
# THE PRIMITIVE REPORTED A FAILURE: the nonzero ABI status of its own fn (lmx_primitive.h.lm1).
# A status of its own ON PURPOSE, and each of the four collisions is refused deliberately: it is
# not business zero (a primitive may return the VALUE 0 with status OK -- that is success, and
# the value rides in `out`/`dest`, never in the status), not LMX_WALK_INVALID (the graph is well
# formed and the record was admitted), not LMX_WALK_UNSUPPORTED (this slice DOES read the node)
# and not LMX_WALK_NO_GRAPH.  It travels up unchanged to whoever mapped the activation; the
# Thread reports it through the Thread ABI's own existing failure status (lmx_thread.lm1).
define: LMX_WALK_PRIMITIVE 6
# Reserved distinct dispatch refusal status; not an empty-body or missing-plan rule.
define: LMX_WALK_NOT_CALLABLE 7
# D-37: a METHOD throw rides as LMX_WALK_THROWN + k so throw 1 is never
# LMX_WALK_INVALID. Walker errors stay 1..7 and become X1 at note_walk_fail.
define: LMX_WALK_THROWN 8

# What lmx_walk_op answers for a frame node whose code is not one of those below.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_UNKNOWN -1
# The discriminators of this slice's roles: the index of a role's record in the roles
# Structure and the `code` of that record.  They are not the identity of a node -- the
# address of the record is -- and they are not an L3 instruction set.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_NONE 0
define: LMX_WALK_OP_RET 1
define: LMX_WALK_OP_CALL 2
define: LMX_WALK_OP_LIT 3
define: LMX_WALK_OP_OWN 4
define: LMX_WALK_OP_ARG 5
define: LMX_WALK_OP_AT 6
define: LMX_WALK_OP_PUT 7
define: LMX_WALK_OP_SET 8
define: LMX_WALK_OP_ADD 9
define: LMX_WALK_OP_SUB 10
define: LMX_WALK_OP_LT 11
define: LMX_WALK_OP_EQ 12
define: LMX_WALK_OP_IF 13
define: LMX_WALK_OP_WHILE 14
define: LMX_WALK_OP_OF 15
# [prim, record, arg ...] -- THE PRIMITIVE INSERT (lmx_primitive.h.lm1).  `record` is a PHYSICAL
# reference to an LmxPrimitive, admitted because the arena classifies it as
# LMX_DOMAIN_KIND_PRIMITIVE -- never because a number in the node says so.  The remaining
# children are its operands, evaluated exactly like a call's arguments.  Appended after the
# slice's roles; the role's identity is still the address of its record, not this number.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_PRIM 16
# [expect_int, path, want] -- type/equality check on a subject's path.  Uses f\args[0]
# as the subject (the input graph), never f\self or own-field semantics.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_EXPECT_INT 17
define: LMX_WALK_OP_DEREF 18
# -177 c4 / D-54: PUT with an evaluated holder (m\f: v through a reference).
define: LMX_WALK_OP_PUT_OF 19
# MUL/DIV/MOD have the same typed operand shape as ADD/SUB. Zero divisor is INVALID.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_MUL 20
define: LMX_WALK_OP_DIV 21
define: LMX_WALK_OP_MOD 22
# [empty]: a new empty Structure, one per execution (`E()`, `m()`, a D-23 empty actual) -- made the way the
# native emission makes one (lmx_node_new_owned); no prototype in the plan (lmx_walk_empty).
define: LMX_WALK_OP_EMPTY 23
# -186: [put_ref, holder, slot, value] -> lmx_arena_ref_store (direct Structure own slot).
# Same operand order as PUT. Mutant: PUT+pointer_store into a direct slot -> RED.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_PUT_REF 24
# -170 c2: array element / length at the walked root (Grok). Contiguous claim after
# PUT_REF; Sonnet MERGE prim takes 28+ (OP_COUNT coord via lmx_uds 2026-09-25).
# [elem, holder, slot, index] / [elemput, holder, slot, index, value] / [length, holder, slot].
# Holder 0 is the current occurrence. Bounds use descriptor.size; char values are
# read from backing bytes, while ADDRESS retains the backing element's place.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_ELEM 25
define: LMX_WALK_OP_ELEMPUT 26
define: LMX_WALK_OP_LENGTH 27
# -201: [pad, param_ref_0 .. param_ref_P-1, body]. Catch landing. Count was 28.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_PAD 28
# User break and continue. A body propagates them. WHILE, FOR and UNTIL consume
# them: break ends the loop as success, continue starts the next turn (FOR runs
# its step first, UNTIL asks its condition). They are not walker errors (1..7)
# and not throws (>= THROWN).
# A jump that escapes the walk is an unknown status.
define: LMX_WALK_BREAK -2
define: LMX_WALK_CONTINUE -3
# Internal Message-stop control, not an error or throw. Activations publish and
# rewind before public run/dispatch normalize it to success with absent result.
define: LMX_WALK_STOPPED -4
define: LMX_WALK_OP_BREAK 29
define: LMX_WALK_OP_CONTINUE 30
# §7b: the working state (the header's THE WORKING STATE).
define: LMX_WALK_OP_OWN_OF 31
define: LMX_WALK_OP_SET_OF 32
define: LMX_WALK_OP_PRIM_PUB 33
# An argument is its parameter (the author, bafca4c; Q52): SET_ARG writes the activation's own value.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_SET_ARG 34
# [exec, 0, S, contract, catch, args...]: evaluate S once and dispatch that
# occurrence using the same declared transport contract as CALL.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_EXEC 35
# [node]: the activation's `node` (book §3) -- its data's parent, the physical lexical space above the method: the
# unit for a file-level method, the host's occurrence for a nested one, the copied lexical context under which a
# returned node was made (a merge result's parent).  OF / PUT_OF go on from it by the slots of that space's body.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_NODE 36
# [admit_as, sourceToken, catchCount, value, targetModel, alternativesCount,
# defaultMapCount, directLayout, fullReceiver, defaultTargetMap[defaultMapCount],
# (layoutToken, targetMap[targetWidth]) * alternativesCount, catchRows...].
# Counts/map entries are inline SIZE_T constants; targetModel is a descriptor.
# Tokens are CHAR_PTR cells holding module-lifetime metadata addresses, never
# raw foreign graph children. Missing source/direct cells mean unknown tokens.
# directLayout is genuine producer evidence; otherwise any completed admission
# of this held value may supply schema identity only, not a map or Consumer proof.
# The default (0 cells = identity, otherwise targetWidth cells) is selected ONLY
# when the held value's known token equals sourceToken.
# Alternatives select by exact layout identity, never by equal partial maps.
# fullReceiver is 1 for ordinary reference/return reception, which checks the
# selected pending map with every receiving field required before publication.
# It is 0 only when the compiler proved this Consumer's used fields. This
# operation-local requirement is not cached as a global Consumer approval.
# Unknown layout uses ordinary admission. An existing target correspondence
# may be reused only after admission for the current receiver; this also applies
# to known unlisted layouts, which cannot guess a map. ImplEntry
# borrows this frame+offset: no correspondence Structure or composed allocation.
# Candidate once; null passes before lookup; NO is the implements throw.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_ADMIT_AS 37
# [and, a, b] / [or, a, b]: `a && b` / `a || b` as one value, short-circuit -- b is evaluated only when a does not decide
# -- an int, 1 or 0.  A condition is then one value however it is built, and a loop asks it afresh in full each turn,
# after a `continue` too.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_AND 38
define: LMX_WALK_OP_OR 39
# [for, cond, body, step]: the core `for` (book, branches and loops: the initialization once, then condition, body and
# step).  The initialization is the step before this node; `step` -- a plain Structure of steps -- runs after each turn
# of the body, a `continue` too, and a `break` ends the loop as success.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_FOR 40
# [until, cond, body]: the postcondition loop (book §13, a closing `until`): the body first, then the condition, and
# the loop ends when it holds -- a `continue` goes to the condition, a `break` ends the loop as success.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_UNTIL 41
# [address, place-expression, closed-pointer-type witness]. Resolve the physical
# place without loading its value or publishing the activation's working state.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_ADDRESS 42
# [self]: the actual data occurrence of this activation (holder zero), not its
# code and not its lexical parent. Internal operand; source `node` stays NODE.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_SELF 43
# Retained source Frames whose bodies are not operands of the L3 evaluator.
# Directives are inert. A reached machine-only operation cannot be interpreted;
# its source tree still exists when its callable has a native implementation.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_SOURCE_INERT 44
define: LMX_WALK_OP_SOURCE_MACHINE 45
# [else, owned-body]: a source sibling of its IF. The IF borrows this
# application for its false arm; the enclosing body owns it. Encountering the
# sibling in ordinary source order does not execute its body a second time.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_ELSE 46
# [named, coordinate, payload]: a named actual at its written place among a
# call's operands. The call evaluates its operands in the order they stand,
# which is the order they were written, and hands each value to the formal
# whose coordinate the operand carries. An operand that is not NAMED supplies
# the formal of its own position. The node's source name is the written name
# of the formal. Outside a call's operands the node is not an expression.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_NAMED 47
# [neg, operand], [pos, operand]: a prefix sign over its one operand. The
# operand is evaluated once and promoted as C promotes it; NEG negates the
# promoted value, POS leaves it. A written prefix stays one operator with one
# operand: it is never a subtraction from an invented zero.
define: LMX_WALK_OP_NEG 48
define: LMX_WALK_OP_POS 49
define: LMX_WALK_OP_COUNT 50
# Source role of an operation, separate from its execution opcode. The shared
# role record encodes source * OP_COUNT + opcode in its existing code word.
# Receiver materialization keeps the real typed cell; no leaf wraps that cell.
# An explicit initializer and an implicit declaration action must not become
# indistinguishable from a later assignment, even if their effects coincide.
define: LMX_WALK_SOURCE_ORDINARY 0
define: LMX_WALK_SOURCE_INITIALIZER 1
define: LMX_WALK_SOURCE_IMPLICIT 2
define: LMX_WALK_SOURCE_ANONYMOUS 3
define: LMX_WALK_SOURCE_TRAILER 4
define: LMX_WALK_SOURCE_COUNT 5
# One temporary value, including an explicitly present null reference. type is the
# closed source type. Numeric values occupy their actual C-width member; reference
# values are already loaded exactly once and their pointees remain opaque.
define: LMX_WALK_VALUE_NUMBER 1
define: LMX_WALK_VALUE_REFERENCE 2
struct: LmxWalkValue
    int: present
    int: kind
    int: type
    @: void ref
    int: number
    size_t: wide
    unsigned: natural
    ulong: longnum
    char: byte
end: LmxWalkValue

# A physical place selected before any load. Cell places name real typed storage;
# descriptor places name the descriptor itself. This is activation-local metadata,
# never a graph or a retained index.
struct: LmxWalkPlace
    @: void address
    int: type
    int: descriptor
end: LmxWalkPlace

# §7b: one row of an activation's working table -- an own field the body uses by a bare name.  The slot
# is where the field is (holder's child `index`); kind 1 is a number (num, of type ty), 2 a pointer cell
# (ref, what it holds), 3 a Structure slot (ref, the Structure or 0).  dirty: an executed write since the
# last publication.  next: the row made after this one.
struct: LmxWalkWork
    @: Lmx holder
    size_t: index
    @@: void slot
    @: void ref
    size_t: num
    int: kind
    int: ty
    int: dirty
    @: LmxWalkWork next
end: LmxWalkWork

# What graph mode needs from its surroundings, for one Message on one thread: the
# Message's arena (to tell a Structure from a cell among the fields of a body), the
# execution context's temporary-frame store, and the program's role records.  Whoever
# runs the turn builds it; this unit only reads it.
struct: LmxWalkContext
    @: LmxArena arena
    @: LmxScratch scratch
    @: Lmx roles
    # Physical address of the ordinary receiver-expression graph value denoting the exact
    # independent+const+immutable profile.  Zero means this program declares no such profile.
    @: Lmx immutable_profile
    # How many times this unit has asked the arena's index what an address is.
    size_t: classified
end: LmxWalkContext

# One activation.  An automatic object of lmx_walk_run; nothing of it is in the graph.
struct: LmxWalkFrame
    @: LmxWalkContext context
    @: LmxArena arena
    @: Lmx roles
    # The one Structure this activation runs (the header's ONE STRUCTURE): `code` is read for its
    # body operators (never written), `node` for its declared fields -- the same M at every call,
    # two references only as an implementation debt of the ABI.  An own-field holder that names
    # `code` means `node` (lmx_walk_data_holder).
    @: Lmx code
    @: Lmx node
    # The declared inputs use value-storage addresses. Zero is an absent input;
    # a present pointer input has storage even when its payload is null.
    # argown provides the activation's stable typed places, never borrowed boxes.
    @@: void args
    size_t: nargs
    @: LmxWalkValue argown
    int: returned
    LmxWalkValue: result
    # -201: set when a CALL/PRIM throw names a pad. 0 means the throw propagates.
    # payload is the thrown record (0 for an implicit throw).
    @: Lmx landing
    @: void payload
    # §7b: the working table the entry loaded (0 before it): nwork rows linked from work, in this activation's
    # scratch slice.
    @: LmxWalkWork work
    size_t: nwork
end: LmxWalkFrame

prototype:
    # Direct activation: args[k] is declared-width value storage, or zero for an
    # absent input. Storage may belong to a caller or scratch; held references
    # are interpreted only by operations consuming their declared category.
    # out may be zero when the caller discards the typed result.
    # Existing merge-model callback: declared descriptor input and descriptor result;
    # owner is the program arena. This callback does not define source head semantics.
    # -177 c1: receiveMessage take. LmxPrimitive.fn = this; PRIM [prim, record] nargs 0;
    # empty inbox -> out 0 OK; else letter\graph. Impl in lmx_thread.lm1 (link closure).
    fn: lmx_walk_mail_take (@: void owner; @@: void refs; size_t: nargs; @: void dest; @@: void out) int
    # -177 c3: receive-if. LmxPrimitive.fn = this; owner = program arena; PRIM [prim, record, model].
    fn: lmx_walk_receive_if (@: void owner; @@: void refs; size_t: nargs; @: void dest; @@: void out) int
    fn: lmx_walk_merge_model (@: void owner; @@: void refs; size_t: nargs; @: void dest; @@: void out) int
    # -180: admit a value already in hand (native B2). PRIM [prim, record, value, model]; owner=program arena.
    # Value null / pointer-null -> out 0 OK; pointer-or-Structure -> implements; else FAIL=1. Letter admits slot 1.
    fn: lmx_walk_admit (@: void owner; @@: void refs; size_t: nargs; @: void dest; @@: void out) int
    fn: lmx_walk_admit_letter (@: void owner; @@: void refs; size_t: nargs; @: void dest; @@: void out) int
    # D-105 (Q39): the admission of a value to a named Structure is the walker's ADMIT_AS op (lmx_walk_admit_op).
    # Item 738 (steps/capture-738.md): the capture of a Structure -- a copy of src's fields fields[0..n) names
    # (req's slots), fresh value cells at req's own slots, the other slots empty, hung under `parent`; recorded in
    # the arena's `implements` table as req's own layout with holes (an empty slot is not carried).  0 on a field
    # that is not a value cell, or on no room. layout is the compiler's schema
    # token for the freshly constructed req-slot layout, or zero when unknown.
    fn: lmx_walk_capture (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx parent; @: Lmx src; @: Lmx req; @: size_t fields; size_t: n; @: void layout) @: Lmx
    # A copy of what a slot holds, as a merge copies data: a number a fresh cell of its type holding its value now, a
    # char included; anything nonnumeric itself. 0 on no room.
    fn: lmx_walk_cell_copy (@: LmxArena arena; @: void cell) @: void
    # CALL and PRIM use the same physical args/return contract for ABI marshalling.
    fn: lmx_walk_run (@: LmxWalkContext context; @: Lmx node; @@: void args; size_t: nargs; @: LmxWalkValue out) int
    # The same typed activation for an internal caller. code/node identify body
    # and selected occurrence; ordinary calls use one complete Structure for both.
    # The result record is copied before activation scratch is released.
    fn: lmx_walk_activate (@: LmxWalkContext context; @: Lmx code; @: Lmx data; @@: void args; size_t: nargs; @: LmxWalkValue result) int
    # Entry (k.4: no plan, no descriptor -- next_core_tasks.md §3 item 9).  Opens the frame
    # over `code`/`data` and asks the arena whether both identify Structures. An empty
    # body remains a valid Structure. Nothing else is looked at or cached; a body
    # node this slice does not read is refused when the body actually runs, not here.
    fn: lmx_walk_enter (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: LmxWalkContext context; @: Lmx code; @: Lmx data; @@: void args; size_t: nargs) int

    # The roles of a program: a plain Structure whose child k is THE record of role k.
    # Opened once per program graph; every frame node refers to these records.
    fn: lmx_walk_roles_open (@: LmxArena arena) @: Lmx
    # Bind the program's shared role table for op dispatch.
    fn: lmx_walk_program_bind (@: Lmx roles) void
    fn: lmx_walk_program_roles () @: Lmx
    # Construction of body nodes, for a translator and for tests.  A node is a fresh
    # Structure of `arena` with `children` slots and immediate structural parent `parent`; a frame
    # node gets the shared record of role `code` in child[0].  The caller stores the node
    # into its parent's slot.
    fn: lmx_walk_frame (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx roles; @: Lmx parent; int: code; size_t: children) @: Lmx
    # Source identity on an existing operation; execution still uses its base opcode.
    fn: lmx_walk_source_mark (@: Lmx roles; @: Lmx operation; int: source) int
    fn: lmx_walk_plain (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx parent; size_t: children) @: Lmx
    fn: lmx_walk_store_size (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx code; size_t: slot; size_t: value) int
    fn: lmx_walk_store_int (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx code; size_t: slot; int: value) int
    fn: lmx_walk_store_char (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx code; size_t: slot; int: value) int
    fn: lmx_walk_store_charptr (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx code; size_t: slot; @: char value) int
    fn: lmx_walk_store_unsigned (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx code; size_t: slot; unsigned: value) int
    fn: lmx_walk_store_ulong (@: LmxArena arena; @: Lmx code; size_t: slot; ulong: value) int

    # §7b: the working state -- the slot an OWN/OWN_OF node names (with its holder and index), the row of a
    # slot, a row loaded, the entry load derived from the code, and the publication of the dirty rows.
    fn: lmx_walk_work_cell (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: void node; int: write; @@: Lmx holder; @: size_t index; @@@: void slot) int
    fn: lmx_walk_work_find (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @@: void slot) @: LmxWalkWork
    fn: lmx_walk_work_make (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: Lmx holder; size_t: index; @@: void slot) int
    fn: lmx_walk_load_node (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: Lmx node) int
    fn: lmx_walk_load_code (@: LmxWalkFrame f) int
    fn: lmx_walk_publish (@: LmxWalkFrame f) int
    # The activation's write of its input k (SET_ARG).
    fn: lmx_walk_arg_write (@: LmxWalkFrame f; size_t: k; int: ty; @: LmxWalkValue value; @: LmxWalkValue out) int
    # Internal steps, named here because they are mutually recursive.
    fn: lmx_walk_kind (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: void p) int
    fn: lmx_walk_op (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: void code) int
    fn: lmx_walk_eval (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: void code; @: LmxWalkValue out) int
    fn: lmx_walk_body (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: Lmx body; size_t: first) int
    fn: lmx_walk_value_clear (@: LmxWalkValue value) void
    fn: lmx_walk_value_ref (@: LmxWalkValue out; int: ty; @: void ref) int
    fn: lmx_walk_value_num (@: LmxWalkValue out; int: ty; size_t: number) int
    fn: lmx_walk_value_number (@: LmxWalkValue value; @: size_t number; @: int ty) int
    fn: lmx_walk_value_storage (@: LmxWalkValue value) @: void
    fn: lmx_walk_value_load (@: void storage; int: ty; @: LmxWalkValue out) int
    fn: lmx_walk_value_cell (@: LmxArena arena; @: void cell; @: LmxWalkValue out) int
    fn: lmx_walk_witness_type (@: LmxArena arena; @: void witness) int
    fn: lmx_walk_place (@: LmxWalkFrame f; @: void node; int: write; @: LmxWalkPlace out) int
    fn: lmx_walk_arg_place (@: LmxWalkFrame f; size_t: k; int: ty; @: LmxWalkPlace out) int
    fn: lmx_walk_value_store (@: LmxWalkPlace place; @: LmxWalkValue value) int
